 "note": "Win B, paired and interleaved: pixelRatio 1.7 (the adaptive scaler's first backoff rung, ratio x STEP_DOWN) against the fixed 2 the renderer used to pin unconditionally. Both arms aa=off. This is what ONE step of the scaler buys on a machine that cannot hold the full ratio; the drawing buffer goes 2560x1440 -> 2176x1224, i.e. 28% fewer pixels, and the GPU saving tracks that almost exactly - which is the evidence that the five-level bloom chain is resolution-bound. Read the paired delta, not the absolutes (tools/perf/README.md)."
}
